 # Sessions
 
+For maintainers of login and checkout, this page describes session lifetime and storage limits. The lifetime was
+extended after members lost orders on slow connections; storage now follows the request to remove session queries.
+
 ## Lifetime
 
 Each request renews the session for 30 minutes, `EXPIRY_MINUTES` in `larder/sessions.py`. Until March 2024 the limit
@@ -9,8 +12,19 @@ minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
 
 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The shared `sessions` instance in `larder/session_store.py` holds sessions in a process-local dictionary
+([keep sessions in the web process](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-web-process.md)). Request handlers must reuse
+that instance. This checkout has no web entry point or request handlers to wire to it.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Separate processes cannot read each other's sessions. Run a single web process or use routing that keeps a member
+  on the same process; routing alone does not solve session loss on restart.
+- Restarts and deploys clear sessions, and existing Postgres sessions are not loaded. Members must sign in again;
+  schedule restarts outside pantry opening hours to reduce disruption.
+- The store does not evict expired entries. Callers remain responsible for checking session lifetime, and memory
+  stays allocated until the process restarts.
 
 ## Shaped by
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+- [Keep sessions in the web process](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-web-process.md)
